# SHA-256 of every upstream file this package ships unmodified from
# libunibreak 8.0 (lightweight tag libunibreak_8_0, commit
# 28a2756b864c343f438cd22537d49d394d4666a5,
# https://github.com/adah1972/libunibreak.git).
#
# 66 records. The set is the upstream-owned entries of build.zig.zon `.paths`:
# the whole src/ directory (45 files: the nine compiled translation units, the
# five installed public headers, the six non-installed internal headers plus
# test_skips.h, the seven generated UCD tables, the three Unicode conformance
# fixtures, upstream's own C harness, upstream's three build-system files, its
# seven generators plus their shared helper, the two sed scripts and the
# linebreakdata template), doc/architecture.md, tools/ (7 files), and 13 root
# files: .clang-format, .mailmap, AUTHORS, Doxyfile, LICENCE, Makefile.am, NEWS,
# README.upstream.md, autogen.sh, bootstrap, configure.ac, libunibreak.pc.in, purge.
# It is a subset of the upstream tree, not a copy of it.
#
# Deliberately absent, each for a stated reason:
#   .gitignore -- upstream's 43 lines are kept verbatim and this fork appends
#   its own 26-line Zig block, so the file is not byte-identical to upstream.
#   Upstream's own bytes, read from the pinned commit's blob, are 549 bytes with
#     bbad54185e3da91dacb7854b544440426c2ff2cf71062995cdcdfd5ea56fae07  .gitignore
#   The working-tree file is that blob's first 43 lines followed by the appended
#   block; the two were compared and the first 43 lines are byte-identical.
#   build.zig, build.zig.zon, cross-test.profile.sh, zig/, tests.zig,
#   smoke.zig, consumer/, .github/workflows/verify.yml, package.nix, flake.nix,
#   flake.lock, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml, .envrc, README.md, UPSTREAM.md,
#   UPSTREAM.sha256, NOTICE.md, README.zig.md, CHANGELOG.md, FORK-NOTES.md,
#   FORK-LICENSE.md -- this fork's own files, itemised in FORK-LICENSE.md. The
#   grant over them is recorded there and is not an upstream grant.
#   flake.lock is in `.paths` because it exists in this tree: it is generated by
#   evaluating flake.nix, not written by hand, and it carries no grant of its own.
#   devenv.lock is absent and stays absent -- no devenv shell has been entered, so
#   there is no lock to ship and inventing one would be a fabrication.
#   README.md was upstream's README at this pin and is this fork's README now; it
#   moved to README.upstream.md with its bytes and its digest unchanged, and the
#   record below names that path. A fork's own README is never an upstream file.
#   LICENCE-UNICODE.txt -- carried Unicode licence text fetched from
#   https://www.unicode.org/license.txt, not an upstream file. It is recorded
#   below with its own digest so a recipient can check it too:
#     e7a93b009565cfce55919a381437ac4db883e9da2126fa28b91d12732bc53d96  LICENCE-UNICODE.txt
#   UPSTREAM.sha256 itself -- a record cannot contain its own digest.
#
# How these digests were produced, and what they are a digest of. Each blob
# of the pinned commit 28a2756b864c343f438cd22537d49d394d4666a5 was read out of
# the clone's object store and hashed as a raw byte read (CPython 3.13.14
# hashlib.sha256) on 2026-10-03, and the result compared against this file's own
# record: 59 compared, 0 disagreements. The pinned tree holds 67 blobs in all --
# these 66 and `.gitignore`.
#   The seven `tools/` blobs below were added when `.paths` began carrying
#   `tools/` whole, because the install step reads `tools/test.txt` out of it.
#   Their digests come from the same pinned-blob extraction, and were read again
#   from the working-tree files on 2026-10-04: all seven agree. No new
#   pinned-object comparison was run for them, so the 59-comparison figure above
#   is a 2026-10-03 observation about 59 records and is not restated as 66.
#
# So this record is a claim about UPSTREAM'S BYTES, not about this working tree:
# every line was derived from the pinned object, not from a file on disk that
# this fork could have edited. It is still not a signature and not a Git object
# id. See UPSTREAM.md, "Integrity", for what it does and does not establish.
#
# Verify with:  sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
